      <p class="section__text">
        Women's fashion moves faster than menswear. Fast fashion brands operate on 52 micro-seasons per year, constantly introducing new styles. For independent brands, this pace is unsustainable and unnecessary. Most successful independent women's brands operate on 2-4 focused collections per year - spring/summer and fall/winter core collections, with possible capsule collections in between. This planned approach allows for quality production without constant pressure.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Production planning around trend cycles is essential. Plan your production timeline backward from your launch date. If launching for spring, start production 90 days in advance to account for sampling, production, and shipping. Build buffer time into your schedule - delays happen. Work with manufacturers who understand women's fashion timelines and can accommodate reasonable rush orders when needed. SDF offers rush production for time-sensitive launches at a 20-30% premium.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Capsule collection strategy works well for small women's brands. Instead of chasing every trend, focus on 4-6 key pieces per season that represent your brand identity. This approach reduces production complexity, lowers risk, and builds brand coherence. Customers remember distinctive pieces, not quantity of options. Quality over quantity builds stronger brands in women's fashion. SDF's 300 piece MOQ supports capsule collection production without excessive inventory commitment.
